RDF 1.2 SEMANTIC FOUNDATION
===========================

COMPLETE CHAIN
---------------------------------------------------------

RDF 1.2 = (exists A + IEXT + IT) + D + RDF vocab + RDFS + Named graphs

L0  Simple Semantics
L1  Datatype Semantics (D-Entailment)
L2  RDF Semantics
L3  RDFS Semantics
L4  Dataset Semantics

RDFTerm
  -> Triple
  -> Graph
  -> exists A
  -> I = (IR, IP, IEXT, IS, IL, IT)
  -> Truth via IEXT
  -> Propositions via IT
  -> D-constraints
  -> RDF conditions
  -> RDFS conditions
  -> Dataset structure
  -> |=

---------------------------------------------------------
TYPES AND FUNDAMENTALS
---------------------------------------------------------

IRI        Internationalized Resource Identifier
BN         Blank Node
Lit        Literal
TT         Triple Term

RDFTerm    = IRI U BN U Lit U TT

Triple     = (s, p, o)
             s in IRI U BN U TT
             p in IRI
             o in RDFTerm

Graph      = Set of Triple

Dataset    = (DefaultGraph, NamedGraphs)

IR         resources (universe)
IP         properties

IEXT       IP -> PowerSet(IR x IR)
IS         IRI -> IR U IP
IL         Lit -> IR          (partial)
IT         IR x IP x IR -> IR (injective)

IPR(I)     = { IT(x, y, z) | x in IR, y in IP, z in IR }
             set of propositions

ICEXT(y)   = { x | <x, y> in IEXT(I(rdf:type)) }
             class extension

A          BN -> IR
             blank node mapping (existential witness)

---------------------------------------------------------
L0  SIMPLE SEMANTICS
---------------------------------------------------------

Simple interpretation:

    I = (IR, IP, IEXT, IS, IL, IT)

Denotation (ground):

    I(literal)     = IL(literal)
    I(IRI)         = IS(IRI)
    I((s,p,o))     = IT(I(s), I(p), I(o))     // triple term

Truth of asserted triple:

    I |= (s p o)
    iff
        I(p) in IP
        and
        (I(s), I(o)) in IEXT(I(p))

Blank nodes:

    [I+A](name)        = I(name)
    [I+A](blank)       = A(blank)
    [I+A]((s,p,o))     = IT([I+A](s), [I+A](p), [I+A](o))

    I |= graph E
    iff
        exists A : BN -> IR
        such that [I+A] makes every triple of E true

Propositions:

    Denotation of any triple (asserted or term) is a proposition
    in IPR(I)

Simple entailment:

    G |= E
    iff
        for all interpretations I:
            I |= G implies I |= E

---------------------------------------------------------
L1  DATATYPE SEMANTICS (D-ENTAILMENT)
---------------------------------------------------------

D-interpretation = simple interpretation recognizing a set D
of datatype IRIs.

For each dt in D:

    L2V_dt : lexical forms -> V(dt)

    IL("lex"^^dt) = L2V_dt(lex)   when well-typed

Ill-typed literals have no denotation.
Any graph containing them is false.

D-entailment:

    G |=_D E
    iff every D-interpretation satisfying G satisfies E

    simple  subset  D-entailment

---------------------------------------------------------
L2  RDF SEMANTICS
---------------------------------------------------------

RDF interpretation (recognizing D) = D-interpretation
satisfying RDF axiomatic triples and:

    x in IP
    iff
        <x, I(rdf:Property)> in IEXT(I(rdf:type))

    and for every recognized datatype IRI aaa in D:

        <x, I(aaa)> in IEXT(I(rdf:type))
        iff x is in the value space of I(aaa)

All RDF interpretations recognize at least:

    { rdf:langString, rdf:dirLangString, xsd:string }

RDF entailment:

    G |=_RDF E

    D-entailment  subset  RDF-entailment

---------------------------------------------------------
L3  RDFS SEMANTICS
---------------------------------------------------------

RDFS interpretation = RDF interpretation
satisfying RDFS axiomatic triples and conditions on ICEXT.

Characteristic conditions:

    <c, d> in IEXT(I(rdfs:subClassOf))
    implies ICEXT(c)subseteq ICEXT(d)

    <p, q> in IEXT(I(rdfs:subPropertyOf))
    implies IEXT(p)subseteq IEXT(q)

    <p, c> in IEXT(I(rdfs:domain))
    and <x, y> in IEXT(p)
    implies x in ICEXT(c)

    <p, c> in IEXT(I(rdfs:range))
    and <x, y> in IEXT(p)
    implies y in ICEXT(c)

Proposition condition:

    exists x, y, z such that IT(x, z, y) = r
    implies
        <r, I(rdfs:Proposition)> in IEXT(I(rdf:type))

Also:

    rdf:reifies rdfs:range rdfs:Proposition

RDFS entailment:

    G |=_RDFS E

    RDF-entailment  subset  RDFS-entailment

---------------------------------------------------------
L4  DATASET SEMANTICS
---------------------------------------------------------

Dataset:

    D = (G0, { (u_i, G_i) })

    G0     default graph
    u_i    graph name (IRI or blank node)
    G_i    named graph

Under simple / RDF / RDFS semantics:

    u_i identifies G_i
    but u_i is not required to denote G_i

    Presence of a named graph does not assert
    the triples of G_i
    and does not entail any "contains" relation

Dataset semantics is orthogonal to L0-L3.
Each graph is interpreted under the chosen entailment regime.

